{
  "note_claim": "UK council tax law has no provision allowing homeowners to avoid council tax by using rooms for private prayer, regardless of religion.",
  "label": "SUPPORTS",
  "quote": "It is not possible for owners of domestic property to avoid council tax by claiming that their property, or part of it, is used for religious purposes.",
  "reason": "The article explicitly states the claim is false and quotes the House of Commons Library confirming no such exemption exists in council tax law."
}
